{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310664,"nonce":"eGstEzUyb1sos4ucrhlUki9igc8=","title":"ROOT-FIXED 2026-07-15 the nondeterministic SIGSEGV where a method with a trailing optional param (e.g. embed(ids, ?mask)) called WITHOUT ...","message":"**Symptom that sent us on a long hunt:** nue BERT `maskTest` (and a minimal `for i { self.embed(ids) }`)\nSIGSEGV'd on the 2nd loop iteration; single embed and two SEQUENTIAL embeds worked; `goldenTest` /\n`textGoldenTest` (embed/embedText 30x in a loop) worked. Looked exactly like a loop/tensor-lifetime\nbug. **It was not.** The loop was a red herring — it just reliably poisoned the garbage ABI slot.\n\n`BertEmbedder.embed(ids:Array\u003cInt\u003e, ?mask:Array\u003cInt\u003e)` has a trailing OPTIONAL param. EVERY caller\n(`self.embed(ids)` with mask omitted) compiled to a **2-arg** call to a **3-param** function\n(`call fn2($self, $ids)`). The omitted `mask` was never filled → on arm64 the callee read **x2**\n(3rd-arg register) = whatever the caller left there. `embed` forwarded it straight to\n`model.embed(ids, mask)` with no null-guard → deref of garbage.\n\nUndefined-behaviour LOTTERY: goldenTest/embedText won it (x2 happened benign/null → `mask != null`\nfalse → skipped). loopRepro's iter-1 LOST it: iter-0's embed left a dangling tensor pointer in x2 →\nnon-null garbage → SIGSEGV. Crash regs nailed it: `x2 = 0xffffffffffffffa1`, faulting read at x8,\n`x1 = 0x600` = 384*4 (a float-row byte size). The MIR showed `call fn2($116, $113)` — 2 args.\n\nTwo gaps stacked:\n1. `function_param_defaults` is only populated when SOME param has an EXPLICIT default\n   (hir_to_mir.rs ~3200 `if defaults.iter().any(|d| d.is_some())`). A bare `?mask` (optional, no\n   default expr) → whole function absent from the map.\n2. More fundamentally, the **instance-method dispatch path** (hir_to_mir.rs ~11377, \"Lower the\n   object (this will be the first parameter)\") builds `method_arg_regs` and calls `build_call_direct`\n   **without ever calling `fill_default_args`** — unlike its sibling static-call (11356) and the\n   other instance path (18042). There are ~362 build_call_direct sites; auditing each is hopeless.\n\n`compiler/src/ir/builder.rs`, in BOTH `build_call_direct` and `build_call_direct_with_type_args`:\nafter arg coercion, if `self.module.functions.contains_key(\u0026func_id)` (in-module/user fn) and\n`args.len() \u003c param_types.len()`, pad the missing trailing params with a type-appropriate default\n(I32(0)/F32/F64/Bool(false)/ else I64(0)=null) built from the callee's OWN signature. Gated to\nin-module funcs so runtime/extern-C calls (always emitted with exact args) are untouched. No-op when\nargs are complete (empty tail slice). One place fixes every one of the 362 call paths.\n\n- Repro (`for i { self.embed(ids) }`) now completes; embed MIR call is now `fn2($self,$ids,$null)` (3 args).\n- BERT: goldenTest \u0026 textGoldenTest 0.9999983 (unchanged), maskTest PASS, tokenizer 32/32.\n- Baseline-vs-fixed diff over 60 unit tests: 59 identical, 1 differs ONLY in map iteration order\n  (benign, same k/v — see [[feedback_regression_output_coherence]]). `test_default_params` correct.\n- llama-chat compiles clean + runs (GGUF load, dispatch OK). clippy -D warnings clean.\n\nRegister forensics beat black-box bisection here. lldb `bt` gave a JIT PC; `RAYZOR_DUMP_FN_PTRS=1`\ncorrelated it; but the DECISIVE evidence was `RAYZOR_DUMP_MIR=1` showing the 2-arg call to a 3-param\nfn, plus `x2 = garbage` in the crash regs. When a crash \"depends on surrounding code / loop shape\"\nand single-vs-loop differs, suspect an UNINITIALIZED/garbage ABI slot (under-filled call), not a\nfree/lifetime bug. Supersedes the earlier wrong hypothesis in [[bugs_interface_dispatch_symbolid_drift_fix]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_optional_arg_unfilled_garbage_abi_slot` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}